<title>USA: Pro-Fac Q3 net profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>Pro-Fac Q3 net profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>ROCHESTER, N.Y. 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>(unaudited)</p>
<p>					  Quarter Ended  9 Months Ended</p>
<p>				 3/29/97    3/23/96  3/29/97  3/23/96</p>
<p> Net sales		  $179,146   $177,849 $561,332 $551,213</p>
<p>Income/(loss)</p>
<p>before taxes, dividends,</p>
<p>allocation of net proceeds</p>
<p>and cumulative effect of</p>
<p>   accounting change	 2,658	  497   13,231  (9,308)</p>
<p>Cumulative effect of</p>
<p>   accounting change(A)	 --	   --    4,606	 --</p>
<p> Net income/(loss)	   1,687    (4,814)   13,123  (2,280)</p>
<p>				 (Data in thousands)</p>
<p>NOTE: Company's full name is Pro-Fac Cooperative.</p>
<p>Pro-Fac Cooperative has preferred stock on the Nasdaq, but no common shares, therefore no per share data appears on earnings statement.</p>
<p>Cumulative effect of accounting change reflects one-time effect of capitalizing manufacturing spare parts instead of expensing as purchased.</p>
<p>Earnings are consolidated with those of Pro-Fac's subsidiary, Curtice-Burns Foods Inc.</p>
